  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 125 PM CDT Fri Jun 5 2026\n\nThe welcomed quiet and comfortable weather we have seen comes to\nan end over the weekend. Continued southerly flow will bring a\nwarming trend across the area through the rest of the forecast \nperiod. Unsettled weather arrives late this weekend and into \nnext week as an upper level disturbance lifts out of the \nsouthern plains. Can't rule out a few isolated showers or storms\non Saturday but believe much of the area will remain dry. \nHigher chances for showers and storms (50-80%) arrive Sunday \ninto Tuesday associated with the passage of an upper trough and \ndiffuse frontal boundary interacting with a moist airmass. PoPs \nthen trend down and further east into Wednesday with mostly dry \nconditions expected the rest of the week as ridging develops \naloft. Increasingly humid conditions arrive during this time as\nwell given the increased moisture in place. High temperatures \nin the upper 80s to lower 90s will work with dewpoints in the \nlow to mid 70s to produce heat indices into the upper 90s to low\n100s.",
